{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06768 - MONDO_5480",
  "verbalization": "Ammonium Lactate appears to be linked to Contact Dermatitis through a series of indirect pathways involving dermatological conditions. The evidence suggests that Ammonium Lactate may act as a mediator in the development of Contact Dermatitis, as it is associated with Granuloma Annulare and Prednicarbate, both of which are indicated to lead to Contact Dermatitis. This implies a potential role for Ammonium Lactate in the pathogenesis of Contact Dermatitis, possibly through its interaction with inflammatory mediators or its influence on the skin's immune response. Additionally, the presence of Ammonium Lactate in the indication for Exanthem (disease), which in turn is linked to Benzoyl Peroxide and Contact Dermatitis, further supports a broader role in dermatological conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex interplay between different agents and their potential contributions to the development of Contact Dermatitis, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the mechanisms underlying these relationships.",
